---
import AppDocLayout from '../../layouts/AppDocLayout.astro';
---

<AppDocLayout
  title="Clacky - Support"
  description="Get help with Clacky - Self-Tape Partner, the iOS app: reading sides, the reader, recording, Clacky's notes, cutting, exporting and the Apple Watch remote."
  ogUrl="https://idlefusion.com/clacky/support"
>
  <main>
    <section class="section-padding">
      <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-8">Support</h1>

        <div class="text-[var(--text-secondary)] leading-relaxed mb-12">
          <p class="text-lg mb-4">Need help with Clacky?</p>
          <p>Send us an email at <a href="mailto:support@idlefusion.com?subject=Clacky%20Support%20Request" class="text-[var(--accent-primary)] hover:underline">support@idlefusion.com</a> and we'll get back to you as soon as we can. Tell us your iPhone model and iOS version. Please don't send your sides; we never need them.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-6">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Clacky didn&rsquo;t find the characters in my sides.</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Clacky looks for a name followed by a line, either &ldquo;JUNE: &hellip;&rdquo; or a name in capitals on its own line above the dialogue. If your sides are laid out differently, open the scene, tap Edit, then Fix the lines, and set who says each line. It takes a few seconds, and Clacky flags names it thinks it misread.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can Clacky read photos of printed or handwritten sides?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Printed pages, screenshots and PDFs work well, even with pencil marks. Handwriting is hit and miss, so check the lines on the cast screen before you roll.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Clacky reads the next line before I&rsquo;ve finished.</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Make sure Clacky waits for you is on (Settings, or the screen before you roll). It listens for you to start speaking and then for a short silence. It works best in a quiet room with the phone within arm&rsquo;s reach. You can always tap Your line or Skip line while rolling.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">The reader is too loud on my tape.</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Clacky&rsquo;s voice plays from your iPhone&rsquo;s speaker and is recorded with you, like a real reader in the room. Reader quieter than you is on by default. Turn your iPhone&rsquo;s volume down a little before you roll for an even quieter reader.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I record audio only?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Choose Audio only on the screen before you roll. Clacky still reads and prompts, and you can export as M4A or WAV.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">What are Clacky&rsquo;s notes based on?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">The line check, eyeline, pickups and level are measured on your iPhone: speech recognition for your lines, the camera frames for where you&rsquo;re looking. On iPhones with Apple Intelligence, Clacky also writes what worked and one thing to try. Notes are suggestions; your choices win.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Which format should I send?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Follow what casting asks for. If they don&rsquo;t say, MP4 at 1080p plays almost everywhere. Turn on Smaller file for sites with upload limits. File names follow Name_Role_Project.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">How do I record my slate and a full-body shot?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Turn on Slate intro first and Full-body shot at the end before you roll, or record them later from Cut it together. Your slate card in Settings fills in what the prompter shows.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Can I combine the best parts of different takes?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. In Cut it together, tap Best of each take and pick a take for each of your lines. Clacky joins them in the middle of the reader&rsquo;s line before, where the cut won&rsquo;t show.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Where are my tapes stored?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">On your iPhone, inside Clacky. Exports go wherever you send them: Files, Photos, AirDrop or Mail. Deleting a scene deletes its takes.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Does Clacky work on Apple Watch?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. When the record screen is open on your iPhone, the watch can roll and stop, shows the take and line, and taps your wrist just before your line. A complication shows your next deadline.</p>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-2">Is Clacky free?</h3>
              <p class="text-[var(--text-secondary)]">Yes. Everything in Clacky is free, with no ads or subscription. If you&rsquo;d like to support it, Settings &rarr; Support Clacky has optional one-time tips. They don&rsquo;t unlock anything, and they&rsquo;re handled entirely by the App Store.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</AppDocLayout>
